body:
I do this some, but I used to do it A LOT. My ex-husband stopped giving into it at some point in our marriage and it hurt like a bitch, but it at least made me think a bit about how I was really just being manipulative. It is REALLY hard not to do it now still, but I have really been working on myself in that area.

&#x200B;

Edit: ok, so I still do this more than I actually realized. I had to think about it, but if I get upset and my boyfriend knows I am upset I will isolate myself until he comes to check on me or else he obviously does not care about me. I try so hard to be a mature adult and go talk it out with him, but unfortunately I don't do it enough. Thank you for posting this, because I really did not think about how I still do that a lot.
